    "description": "<p><strong>Rainy</strong> is more typical of an intense tropical storm, as in the raindrops being liable to cause physical pain because they're so big and fast. Water-Types unanimously excel in rain, but their Electric archenemy finds it easier to deal with them.</p><p><span style='text-decoration: underline;'><strong><span style='text-decoration: underline;'>Effects:</span></strong></span></p><ul><li><p>Water-Type Attacks deal 30% more damage, and Fire-Type Attacks deal 30% less damage.</p></li><li><p>Non-[Contact] Electric-Type Attacks have +30% Range (minimum +1).</p></li><li><p>All creatures resist [Explode] Attacks one step further.</p></li><li><p>All Water-Type creatures gain a bonus to their Overland Allowance equal to 60% of their Swim Allowance (minimum 2).</p></li><li><p>Physical-Category Attacks suffer an additional -1 ACC from RIP.</p></li></ul>"
  },
